---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="privacy" description="Privacy policy for Blab Bun.">
  <main class="mx-auto min-h-[60vh] w-full max-w-[680px] flex-1 px-8">
    <div class="animate-[fadeIn_0.2s_ease]">
      <!-- back -->
      <a
        href="/"
        class="mb-7 inline-block text-[0.76rem] text-[var(--accent)] no-underline"
      >
        ← back
      </a>

      <!-- title -->
      <h1 class="mt-5 mb-6 text-[1.05rem] font-semibold">privacy</h1>

      <!-- content -->
      <div
        class="max-w-[540px] space-y-3.5 text-[0.82rem] leading-[1.9] text-[var(--muted)]"
      >
        <p>
          i don&apos;t collect your personal data in any creepy way. there *is*
          basic analytics running (shoutout cloudflare) but it&apos;s the boring
          kind — just general traffic stats, not “who you are, where you live,
          what you had for lunch” type stuff.
        </p>

        <p>
          if you subscribe to the newsletter, i get your email address and
          that&apos;s it. i&apos;m not selling it, renting it, or doing anything
          weird with it. you&apos;ll just get the occasional post when i
          remember this blog exists.
        </p>

        <p>
          comments aren&apos;t stored in your browser anymore — they&apos;re
          saved in a database (supabase gang). they&apos;re still anonymous
          though, unless you decide to expose yourself in the comment box which
          is between you and your future self.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
